==== OEM Easy Installation ====
**Installing OpenWrt Firmware**

The method for installing OpenWrt firmware using the OEM WebUI is discussed [[:docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing#four_installation_methods|here]]. This method only worked with earlier versions of the OEM firmware. If your router firmware has been upgraded beyond v1.13b03, this method will **not** work. However, the D-Link DIR-885L bootloader contains a **recovery mode**, which can be used to install OpenWrt firmware. 

  - Download OpenWrt firmware to computer. All stable versions of OpenWrt (BCM53xx/generic) can be found [[https://downloads.openwrt.org/|here]].
  - Place router in [[docs:guide-user:installation:recovery_methods:d-link_recovery_gui#accessing_the_recovery_mode|recovery mode]].
  - Upload OpenWrt firmware to router.
  - Configure computer to use DHCP and browse to 192.168.1.1.
  - In LuCI, reset to defaults.
  - In LuCI, upload same firmware again (untick the //keep settings// option).
  - In LuCI, reset to defaults and reboot.
  - Configure OpenWrt as required.

**Restoring OEM Firmware**

Recovery mode can also be used to restore the OEM firmware. As discussed [[:docs:guide-user:installation:recovery_methods:d-link_recovery_gui#about_encrypted_firmwares|here]], in 2018 D-Link started adding a layer of encryption to their stock firmware files. This now requires the OEM firmware file to be decrypted before it can be installed using recovery mode, **or** a //transitional// version of the OEM firmware must be installed first. Unfortunately, the D-Link DIR-885L firmware files can not be decrypted using the [[https://github.com/0xricksanchez/dlink-decrypt|dlink-decrypt]] method. However, they have been successfully decrypted using the method presented [[https://thottysploity.github.io/posts/dir-842/|here]]. As this latter decryption method requires the use of transitional OEM firmware, the following uses the latter restoration process (i.e., simply installs the transitional OEM firmware first).

  - Download OEM firmware (v1.13b03 and v1.21b03_beta01_k24b) from [[https://legacy.us.dlink.com/pages/product.aspx?id=917816fe412e4ef2ada6113374a795b0|here]], **or** (v1.15b02 and v1.20b02) from [[https://eu.dlink.com/uk/en/products/dir-885l-ac3150-mumimo-ultra-wifi-router|here]].
  - Place router in [[docs:guide-user:installation:recovery_methods:d-link_recovery_gui#accessing_the_recovery_mode|recovery mode]].
  - Upload transitional OEM firmware (v1.13b03 **or** v1.15b02).
  - Configure computer to use DHCP and browse to 192.168.1.1.
  - In OEM WebUI, reset to defaults.
  - In OEM WebUI, upload latest encrypted OEM firmware (v1.20b02 **or** v1.21b03).
  - In OEM WebUI, reset to defaults and reboot.
  - Restore saved configuration.

