===== Basic Configuration =====
Extensive configuration information can be found in the OpenWrt [[:docs:guide-user:start#user_guide|documentation]], which contains generic user guides regarding its [[docs:guide-user:base-system:start|basic configuration]], as well as other [[:docs:guide-quick-start:start#quick_start_guide_for_openwrt_installation|quick start guides]].

By default, installation of the pre-built OpenWrt firmware image for the D-Link DIR-885L includes only minimal configuration of the DHCP server and leaves the router's Wi-Fi radios disabled. As a result, additional configuration is required for the D-Link DIR-885L to be used as even the most basic wired or wireless router. Although OpenWrt can be configured exclusively via its [[:docs:guide-user:base-system:user.beginner.cli#command-line_interpreter|CLI]] over SSH, the D-Link DIR-885L can also be configured via the standard OpenWrt WebUI (LuCI), which is included in its pre-built firmware image. To facilitate first-time OpenWrt users, the configuration instructions presented below use LuCI, when possible. Instructions using the CLI are only presented when doing so greatly simplifies the process.
==== Initial Setup ====
The following assumes that the user is familiar with their network layout and has a basic understanding of the settings required to properly configure a network router. Throughout the process remember to click ''Save'' and ''Save & Apply'', when required. 
  - **Password** — go to **System → Administration** and set **Router Password**.
  - **Timezone** — go to **System → System** and in **System Properties → General Settings** select correct ''Timezone''. 
  - **LAN Configuration** — go to **Network → Interfaces** and click ''Edit'' for **lan** Interface:
    - In **General Settings**, change ''IPv4 address'' (optional).
    - In **Advanced Settings**, add DNS server addresses to ''Use custom DNS servers''.
    - In **DHCP Server → Advanced Settings**, add DNS server addresses to ''DHCP-Options'' (optional, see example).
  - ** WAN Configuration** — go to **Network → Interfaces** and click ''Edit'' for **wan** Interface:
    - In **General Settings**, select required ''Protocol'' and add related settings (e.g., ''IPv4 address'', ''IPv4 gateway'').
    - In **System → Reboot**, click ''Perform reboot''.
  - **Wireless Configuration** — go to **Network → Wireless** and click ''Edit'' for **radio0** (i.e., 2.4 GHz band).
    - In **Device Configuration → Advanced Settings**, select correct ''Country Code''.
    - In **Interface Configuration → General Setup**, change ''ESSID'' (optional).
    - In **Interface Configuration → Wireless Security**, select desired ''Encryption'' and ''Cipher'', and enter a ''Key'' (i.e., password).
    - Finally, in **Device Configuration → General Setup**, click ''Enable''.
    - Repeat for **radio1** (i.e., 5.0 GHz band).
  - **LED Configuration** — go to **System → LED Configuration** and click ''Add LED action''.
    - Enter a ''Name'', and select desired ''LED Name'', ''Trigger'', ''Device'' and ''Trigger Mode''.
    - Repeat for other LEDs.

==== H/W Ver: A1 — 5.0 GHz Issues====
The pre-built OpenWrt firmware image for the D-Link DIR-885L includes the radio firmware (blob) for the Broadcom BCM4366B chip. Early OpenWrt releases (17.01.1 through 18.06.9) included an older version of this Broadcom radio firmware (Version: 10.10.69.237, Date: 2016-01-08, File Size: 989,401). However, since OpenWrt release 19.07.0, a newer version of the Broadcom radio firmware has been included (Version: 10.28.2, Date: 2018-11-05, File Size: 1,105,361). As discussed [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/d-link-885l-r-a2-openwrt-18-06-2-upgrade/30523/8|here]] and [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/openwrt-22-03-5-fifth-service-release/159135/76|here]], there appear to be issues with this newer version of the Broadcom radio firmware, which prevent wireless devices from connecting, or staying connected, to the D-Link DIR-885L, when using the 5.0 GHz band. This can be resolved by downloading and manually installing an older version of the Broadcom radio firmware. The current //best candidate// can be found [[https://github.com/hurrian/ea9500_openwrt/tree/master/package/brcmfmac-firmware-4366b1-pcie-panamera/files|here]] (Version: 10.10.122.45, Date: 2017-05-31, File Size: 1,146,907, MD5 Hash: 92d1baab27d88b3ff1c9b9a39c33b0b4).

To replace the current version of the Broadcom radio firmware:
  - Download file (**brcmfmac4366b-pcie.bin**) to computer.
  - Check file size and hash, to ensure it wasn’t corrupted during download.
  - Transfer file to **/lib/firmware/brcm** directory on router (e.g., using SCP).
  - Reboot router.
==== H/W Ver: A2 — Radio Firmware====
The pre-built OpenWrt firmware image only supports hardware version A1 of the D-Link DIR-885L. However, the OpenWrt firmware can be used with hardware version A2 by manually installing the radio firmware (blob) for the Broadcom BCM4366C chip.

To install OpenWrt firmware on the A2 hardware version of the D-Link DIR-885L:

  - Install pre-built OpenWrt firmware image for D-Link DIR-885L.
  - Configure OpenWrt **LAN** and **WAN** Interfaces so that Internet access is available (see above).   
  - Go to **System → Software** and click ''Update lists...''.
     - Once package list has updated, enter //4366// in ''Filter'' field. 
     - For **brcmfmac-firmware-4366c0-pcie**, click ''Install...''.
     - Reboot router.
  - Configure OpenWrt **Wireless** radios (see above).

