==== Buttons ====
General information regarding the use and configuration of hardware buttons is presented [[docs:guide-user:hardware:hardware.button|here]]. The D-Link DIR-885L has two buttons and a slide switch that are inputs to the CPU. The latching power button appears to be hardwired into the power circuit on the PCB. The pre-built OpenWrt firmware image for the D-Link DIR-885L appears to be configured so that the RESET button initiates a //factory reset// (i.e., restores the OpenWrt firmware to its default configuration). The WPS button and ROUTER / EXTENDER slide switch are not pre-configured.
^ Button / Switch     ^ Event   ^ GPIO  ^
| RESET               |  reset  |   17  |
| WPS                 |   wps   |    7  |
| ROUTER / EXTENDER   |    -    |   10  |

