==== Serial ====
{{:media:dlink:dir-885l:dir-885l_serial.jpg?400|Serial Port}}

General information regarding Serial ports and cables is provided [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial|here]]. Located on the top side of the D-Link DIR-885L PCB is an unpopulated 4-pin header labelled JP1. This header is accessible without removing the top heatsink. When probed with a multi-meter, the results do not match the provided general information. However, this header still appears to be a serial port, with the following arrangement: Pin 1 (square) - Rx, Pin 2 - Vcc (3v3), Pin 3 - Gnd, and Pin 4 - Tx. In order to use it reliably, pins should be soldered to the header. **Caution:** This port operates at TTL voltage levels (3v3). Applying voltages greater than 3v3 will permanently damage the router.

^  Serial Port Settings             ||
| Speed                  | 115200    |
| Data Bits              | 8         |
| Stop Bits              | 1         |
| Parity                 | None      |
| Flow Control           | None      |
|                        |           |
|                        |           |

**Note:** The console of the D-Link DIR-885L OEM firmware prior to v1.15b02 is **not** password protected. However, credentials are required to login into the console of later encrypted versions of this firmware. FIXME Please add them, if known.
==== JTAG ====
{{:media:dlink:dir-885l:dir-885l_j1_header.jpg?400|J1 Header}}

General information regarding JTAB ports and cables is provided [[docs:techref:hardware:port.jtag|here]]. Located on the top side of the D-Link DIR-885L PCB is what appears be to a 10-pin header labelled J1. This header is only accessible once the top heatsink has been removed. When probed with a multi-meter, all odd numbered pins appear to be connected to ground, and all even numbered pins give a reading of 3.26 Vdc. Given these results, it's most likely that this is a power connection, used for testing during the manufacturing process. As there are no other headers on the PCB (suitable or otherwise), it appears that the D-Link DIR-885L does not have a JTAB port.
